cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below and also cite the source cohort datasets listed under data/DATA_MANIFEST.md."
title: "Cross-Cohort Reproducibility of Knosp Grade Associations With Incomplete Resection After Pituitary Surgery: analysis code and canonical outputs"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis pipeline (STROBE-reported secondary analysis) for two
  independent, publicly available, de-identified pituitary-surgery cohorts
  (Taiwan index; Spain replication). Firth penalized logistic regression of
  Knosp grade on incomplete resection, model-adjusted absolute risk by
  individual-level g-computation with a 1000-replicate patient bootstrap, and
  exploratory negative-binomial length-of-stay models with Knosp x cohort
  interaction and leave-one-out influence diagnostics.
